---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CRITERIA } from '../../lib/review-score.js';
---
<Base title="How we score electric vans" description="How the Loadspace data score works: five published specs, each scored 1 to 5, averaged. No road-test impressions, no sponsorship.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> › <a href="/reviews/">Reviews</a></div>
    <article class="prose">
      <h1>How we score electric vans</h1>
      <p class="lede">Our reviews have two parts: a summary of what the UK's van testers say, and a Loadspace data score worked out only from facts the maker publishes.</p>

      <h2>What the testers say</h2>
      <p>We read the published UK reviews from established titles and sum them up in our own words. We always say who thinks what, and we check every opinion we report against the review it came from. Where testers disagree, we say so. We haven't driven these vans ourselves, and we say that on every review.</p>

      <h2>The Loadspace data score</h2>
      <p>Opinions vary, so the score sticks to numbers anyone can check. We score five things from 1 to 5, then take the average. Each figure is checked against its source before publishing, using the maker's own price list or spec sheet wherever we can.</p>
      <ul>
        {CRITERIA.map((c) => <li><strong>{c.label}:</strong> {c.what.charAt(0).toLowerCase() + c.what.slice(1)}.</li>)}
      </ul>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th class="num">Score</th>{CRITERIA.map((c) => <th>{c.label}</th>)}</tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {[5, 4, 3, 2, 1].map((pts) => (
              <tr><td class="num"><strong>{pts}</strong></td>{CRITERIA.map((c) => <td class="small">{c.bands.find(([, p]) => p === pts)?.[0]}</td>)}</tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2>What the score leaves out</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Driving and comfort.</strong> These are opinions, so they're in the testers' summary rather than the score.</li>
        <li><strong>Real-world range.</strong> It depends on load, weather and roads. We score the official figure so every van is measured the same way.</li>
        <li><strong>Reliability.</strong> MOT data is useful, but older figures often cover a previous model or the diesel version. We show it on each van's buyer's guide instead of scoring it.</li>
        <li><strong>Lease prices.</strong> They change weekly. Use the <a href="/tools/lease-true-cost/">lease true cost calculator</a> on any deal you're offered.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Independence</h2>
      <p>No maker or dealer pays for a review or sees it before it's published. If we ever earn money from a link on a review page, we'll say so on that page.</p>
      <p class="small"><a href="/reviews/">All reviews →</a></p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
